hands-on/
_build/
# Spark 4's ArtifactManager creates ./artifacts/spark-<uuid>/ in the DRIVER'S CWD on the first job.
# In a notebook the CWD is the lesson's own directory, so this lands inside materials/. The path is
# a hardcoded relative literal in ArtifactManager — no spark conf moves it (spark.driver.artifact.
# localDir does not exist in Spark 4.0). MyST already excludes it (see builder/myst.py EXCLUDE);
# this keeps it out of the student's clone too.
artifacts/
.env
# Each participant's own key file (secrets/bigquery-key.json): never committed.
secrets/
.venv/
__pycache__/
# Measurement reports are written at RUNTIME by `measure` into /workspace/reports/ (one dir per run);
# they are local artifacts, never authored source — keep them out of the student's clone.
reports/
# Vendored dataset dumps stay out of the student repo: each lab's `fetch-seed.sh` downloads them
# (pinned and checksummed) before the lab starts. They are named, never matched by a blanket
# `labs/*/seed/*.sql`: every other file in a seed directory is authored initdb source, and a course
# published without it still comes up "healthy" — with the database that file creates missing
# (`tests/test_seed_ships.py`).
labs/*/seed/01-pagila-schema.sql
labs/*/seed/02-pagila-data.sql
